:\"https://search.cnbc.com/rs/search/combinedcms/view.xml?partnerId=wrss01&id=100003114\",\"feedTitle\":\"US Top News and Analysis\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=cnbc.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Business\",\"title\":\"OpenAI appoints two new members to board of directors\",\"link\":\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/07/21/openai-appoints-two-new-members-to-board-of-directors.html\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cnbc.com%2F2026%2F07%2F21%2Fopenai-appoints-two-new-members-to-board-of-directors.html&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dcnbc.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-21T21:22:32.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"OpenAI appointed longtime financial executives David Vélez and Robin Vince to its nonprofit and for-profit boards.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Hacker News\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=news.ycombinator.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Tech\",\"title\":\"\\\"Drawing\\\" the Mona Lisa with GPT-5.6, Claude, Gemini, and Grok\",\"link\":\"https://www.tryai.dev/blog/ai-drawing-arena-colored-pencils-claude-gpt-grok\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tryai.dev%2Fblog%2Fai-drawing-arena-colored-pencils-claude-gpt-grok&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dnews.ycombinator.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-21T21:13:20.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Comments\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Hacker News\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=news.ycombinator.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Tech\",\"title\":\"A digestion of the Jacobian conjecture counterexample\",\"link\":\"https://terrytao.wordpress.com/2026/07/21/a-digestion-of-the-jacobian-conjecture-counterexample/\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fterrytao.wordpress.com%2F2026%2F07%2F21%2Fa-digestion-of-the-jacobian-conjecture-counterexample%2F&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dnews.ycombinator.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-21T21:09:25.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Comments\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://feeds.content.dowjones.io/public/rss/RSSMarketsMain\",\"feedTitle\":\"WSJ.com: Markets\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=wsj.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"Tech Stocks Return to Rally Mode Ahead of Earnings\",\"link\":\"https://www.wsj.com/finance/stocks/tech-stocks-return-to-rally-mode-ahead-of-earnings-3702d559?mod=rss_markets_main\",\"image\":\"https://images.wsj.net/im-96984716\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-21T21:08:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"Angel Garcia/Bloomberg News\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/feed/\",\"feedTitle\":\"UpgradedPoints.com\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=upgradedpoints.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Others\",\"title\":\"3 Ways To Use the Chase Sapphire Preferred’s 100K Bonus for a Greece Vacation\",\"link\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/100k-chase-sapphire-preferred-greece/\",\"image\":\"https://upgradedpoints.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/02/Chase-Sapphire-Preferred-Marble-Upgraded-Points-LLC.jpeg\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-21T21:00:00.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"The limited-time return of the Chase Sapphire Preferred® Card ‘s 100,000-point bonus offer opens up the door for a lot of travel possibilities. Whether you’re like me and planning your honeymoon many months in advance or looking ahead to next summer’s vacation, applying during an elevated welcome offer can give you that head start. One destination that’s top of mind is Greece. My fiancé has extended family there, so we’re strongly considering spending a few weeks island-hopping and exploring different parts of the country before the peak summer season. The good news is that 100,000 Chase Ultimate Rewards points can go a long way toward making any next trip happen. From flights to hotels, there are several ways to mix and match your points to stretch their value. Earn 100K Bonus Points With the Chase Sapphire Preferred Card The best-ever 100,000-point bonus offer on the Chase Sapphire Preferred card returned in mid-June, and it’s officially ending soon . Currently, eligible new applicants can earn 100,000 bonus points after spending $5,000 in the first 3 months of account opening. That breaks down to $1,667 in monthly spending during the initial window to earn this massive haul of points. After you meet these spending terms, it can take 1 or 2 billing cycles for these points to be reflected in your balance. For many applicants, that means those 100,000 points may not realistically be available until late 2026. But don’t forget you’re also accruing points on any of the card’s bonus categories as you meet that spending minimum . As the card offers 2x to 5x points on popular travel and everyday spending categories, it’s more than possible to reach a rough balance of 120,000 points (or more) quickly. While that sounds like a long wait, it’s actually great timing for prospective travel bookings in 2027. Award availability for flights and hotels is often best when searching 8 to 12 months in advance , especially for popular summer destinations. In fact, planning ahead is often the key to finding the best redemptions before everyone else starts searching. So whether you want to put those points toward flights to Greece, several hotel nights on islands like Santorini, or maybe a combination of both, here are a few ideas to consider. » Related: The Fan-Favorite Chase Sapphire Preferred Card Adds New Perks but Devalues Hyatt Transfers 1. Book 2 Round-Trip Flights to Greece International flights are often the most expensive part of any trip, but 100,000 points can go a long way toward that, so you can free up your budget for special experiences when you land. Chase Ultimate Rewards points transfer to all of its airline partners at a 1:1 ratio, so 100,000 points can turn into 100,000 eligible airline miles with any of the participants. Since virtually all trips to Greece start in Athens, you can book 2 round-trip tickets on Delta’s nonstop flight from Boston (BOS) or New York (JFK) to Athens (ATH) for exactly 120,000 points and around $200 in taxes and fees. Current points rates per round-trip ticket. Image Credit: Virgin Atlantic Although Delta isn’t a direct Chase transfer partner, you can still use Chase points to book Delta-operated flights by transferring them to partner programs Virgin Atlantic Flying Club or Air France-KLM Flying Blue . One of the best sweet spots is through Virgin Atlantic Flying Club, which charges just 30,000 points plus $5.60 in taxes and fees for a one-way Delta flight to Athens . Better yet, Chase periodically offers transfer bonuses to Virgin Atlantic, sometimes as high as 40% . If you can take advantage of one of those promotions, those same 2 round-trip tickets could cost as few as 86,000 Chase Ultimate Rewards points , leaving you with thousands of points to spare. Hot Tip: Learn why I wait until the first of each month before transferring points over to partners. This could help you time the next transfer bonus promotion. 2. Book 4 Nights in Santorini World of Hyatt remains Chase’s most valuable transfer partner, even though it’s now the only partner that no longer transfers at a standard 1:1 ratio . (Eligible new Chase Sapphire Preferred cardholders now get a 4:3 transfer ratio to Hyatt, while existing cardholders who opened their accounts before June 15, 2026, can still transfer 1:1 but move to that same ratio beginning October 1, 2026.) Though the math isn’t as clean as it was before, 120,000 points still yield 90,000 points to Hyatt. And since World of Hyatt’s points rates are some of the most affordable of any hotel program, that’s still a great deal for a trip to Greece. You could transfer 107,000 Chase Ultimate Rewards points to World of Hyatt and use them to book 4 nights at Magma Resort Santorini , a stunning luxury property with just 59 guest rooms. Each of Magma Resort Santorini’s 25 suites has its own private pool. Image Credit: Hyatt With award rates starting at 20,000 Hyatt points per night , this redemption could help you avoid paying more than $400 per night in cash. Even better, a daily breakfast buffet is included for all guests. 3. Splurge on Round-Trip Business Class Flights This final strategy requires a bit more planning than simply applying for 1 card, but it can be well worth the effort if you’re hoping to splurge on a once-in-a-lifetime trip. One of the best points strategies for couples is for both partners to apply for the Chase Sapphire Preferred card . At a $95 annual fee per card, it’s an affordable way to earn a substantial amount of points, and the card offers plenty of ongoing value and benefits to help justify the cost. If both partners qualify for the credit card and meet the spending requirement, you earn a combined 200,000 Chase Ultimate Rewards points from the welcome offers alone. If you’re planning your trip many months in advance, you also have plenty of time to earn even more points through everyday spending. A SWISS business class cabin. Image Credit: Ehsan Haque One of the biggest advantages of Chase Ultimate Rewards is that members of the same household can combine their points into a single account . Pooling your rewards makes it much easier to book flights or hotel stays together and maximize the value of your points. Out of all of the Chase transfer partners, Air Canada Aeroplan has the best points rates for business class flights to Europe . Even though business class rates are much pricier, that once-in-a-lifetime experience may be worth it for a really special trip. For example, a one-way ticket from Newark (EWR) to Athens with a day layover in Zurich (ZRH) — for 75,000 points in SWISS business class : Use Chase’s airline partners for more flight options to Europe. Image Credit: Aeroplan Of course, that means it’d cost 150,000 points to book round-trip tickets for each person (but perhaps less with a transfer bonus). Even so, this isn’t such a lofty goal once you consider the 100,000-point bonus offer, plus diligently saving up more points over the months. The Chase Sapphire Preferred card makes it easy by rewarding 5x points on Chase Travel , 3x points on dining, gas and EV charging , some streaming services, vacation homes, and online groceries, 2x points on all other travel, and 1x points on everything else. It offers one of the most diverse bonus categories of any popular rewards card. Final Thoughts This current 100,000-point welcome offer on the Chase Sapphire Preferred card is one of the best opportunities we’ve seen in 2026 to reduce the cost of a long-haul trip. And that’s before factoring in the card’s ongoing benefits, which include a statement credit for Global Entry, TSA PreCheck, or NEXUS, an annual $100 Chase Travel hotel credit, and no foreign transaction fees.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://seekingalpha.com/tag/etf-portfolio-strategy.xml\",\"feedTitle\":\"ETFs & Portfolio Strategy Articles on Seeking Alpha\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=seekingalpha.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Investing\",\"title\":\"VRP: Preferred ETF Mitigating Interest Rate Risk\",\"link\":\"https://seekingalpha.com/article/4923931-vrp-preferred-etf-mitigating-interest-rate-risk?source=feed_tag_etf_portfolio_strategy\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fseekingalpha.com%2Farticle%2F4923931-vrp-preferred-etf-mitigating-interest-rate-risk%3Fsource%3Dfeed_tag_etf_portfolio_strategy&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dseekingalpha.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-21T20:58:16.000Z\",\"createDate\":null,\"content\":\"\",\"re