ough November 30, 2026 , and includes flights originating at Etihad’s U.S. gateways , which are Atlanta (ATL), Boston (BOS), Charlotte (CLT), Chicago (ORD), New York (JFK), and Washington, D.C. (IAD). This sale doesn’t cover every city Etihad flies to, unfortunately. The destinations focus on the Middle East and the Indian subcontinent. Luckily, the sale page makes it easy to see offers from your departure point, and changing the departure city to see other offers is easy. You can also view offers for both economy and business class. Offers we’re seeing include: Round-trip economy offers Abu Dhabi, UAE, for $670 from New York Bangkok for $869 from Boston Nairobi, Kenya, for $1,099 from Charlotte Round-trip business fares Colombo, Sri Lanka, for $3,839 from Washington, D.C. Multiple cities in India starting at $2,650 from Chicago Abu Dhabi for $4,399 from Atlanta Etihad business class on the A380. Image Credit: Daniel Ross Passengers can add a stopover package during the booking process that includes a complimentary stay at select hotels across Abu Dhabi. Stopover packages must be booked directly with Etihad, either through its website or mobile app ( iOS and Android ). If you’re interested in taking advantage of this sale, book your flight using a travel rewards credit card with bonus points on airfare and travel purchases. Some of our favorites here at Upgraded Points include the Platinum Card ®  from American Express , the  Chase Sapphire Reserve ® , and the  Capital One Venture X Rewards Credit Card . Hot Tip: Remember that Etihad recently reduced status qualification requirements by 25% and is waiving change and cancellation fees on many flights. Those could be extra incentives to jump on this sale. Final Thoughts Abu Dhabi-based Etihad is advertising discounted economy and business-class tickets to cities in the Middle East, India, Kenya, and beyond. Discounts of up to 20% apply to flights from Etihad’s U.S. departure airports, but you need to book by July 26 and fly by November 30 to enjoy this offer.\",\"replyCount\":0,\"viewCount\":0},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://voz.vn/f/diem-bao.33/index.rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Điểm báo\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=voz.vn&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Forum\",\"title\":\"[Dịch] Nga: Điện Kremlin lần đầu tiên bình luận về các cuộc tấn công vào kho hàng của Wildberries: \\\"Tình hình quả thực đang rất khó khăn\\\"\",\"link\":\"https://voz.vn/t/dich-nga-dien-kremlin-lan-dau-tien-binh-luan-ve-cac-cuoc-tan-cong-vao-kho-hang-cua-wildberries-tinh-hinh-qua-thuc-dang-rat-kho-khan.1262601/unread\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fvoz.vn%2Ft%2Fdich-nga-dien-kremlin-lan-dau-tien-binh-luan-ve-cac-cuoc-tan-cong-vao-kho-hang-cua-wildberries-tinh-hinh-qua-thuc-dang-rat-kho-khan.1262601&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dvoz.vn%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-21T13:51:44.000Z\",\"createDate\":\"2026-07-21T20:45:05+0700\",\"content\":\"Chính phủ Nga đang \\\"giữ liên lạc\\\" với công ty Wildberries sau đợt tấn công bằng máy bay không người lái của Ukraine vào các kho vận chuyển của hãng. Phát ngôn viên của Tổng thống Nga - ông Dmitry Peskov đã đưa ra tuyên bố này. \\\"Tình hình thực sự khó khăn do những thiệt hại mà cả công ty lẫn các doanh nghiệp vừa và nhỏ phải chịu. Chính phủ đang xử lý vấn đề này. Tất nhiên đối với các thông tin chi tiết tốt nhất nên liên hệ với Nội các Bộ trưởng. Dù vậy Chính phủ vẫn đang duy trì... Click to expand... Read more\",\"replyCount\":95,\"viewCount\":7000},{\"feedUrl\":\"https://news.ycombinator.com/rss\",\"feedTitle\":\"Hacker News\",\"feedIcon\":\"https://www.google.com/s2/favicons?domain=news.ycombinator.com&sz=64\",\"feedCategory\":\"Tech\",\"title\":\"PCjs Machines\",\"link\":\"https://www.pcjs.org/\",\"image\":\"/api/og-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.pcjs.org%2F&rss=&icon=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.google.com%2Fs2%2Ffavicons%3Fdomain%3Dnews.ycombinator.com%26sz%3D64\",\"pubDate\":\"2026-07-21T13:48:35.000Z\",\"cr